wait wait wait... what's the idea behind this feature? If you want this to happen:

```ts
class Entity {
  @Column() title: string;

  @BeforeInsert() beforeInsert() {
    // not called for plain object saves
  }
}
...
getRepository<Entity>.save({ title: "foo" })
```

Then of course it won't happen and it should not happen. It's not appropriate even trying fix this issue. No instance - no method to call. You should not try to call method of non-exist instance.

Solution to the user-facing problem is:

```ts
repository.save(repository.create({ title: "foo" })) // also make sure entity initialization doesn't have side effects if you want just to update the entity, e.g. no initialized properties. 
```

If you ask if we should do it by ourself in the `save` method - the answer is no, because we never know about side effects in user entity.

